  <item>
    <title>在失控的试管经历中，认识自己学习交托</title>
    <link>https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episode/66c2bf6133591c27be15cd21</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">66c2bf6133591c27be15cd21</guid>
    <pubDate>Mon, 19 Aug 2024 03:43:29 +0000</pubDate>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><span>四个月没更新，大家都以为这个节目黄了，但猫三又回来了。这一集，她讲述了过去几个月试管备孕的失败经历给她带来的巨大伤痛，以及她在疗伤过程中学到的受用一生的功课：认识自己和学习交托。</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="242">04:02</a> 第三次试管取卵失败，总结过去一年试管备孕经历。</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="481">08:01</a> 怀孕生育是上帝的事儿，人类的计划再严丝合缝都会显得漏洞百出</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="773">12:53</a> 把不可掌控之事交托给上帝，谈何容易！</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="906">15:06</a> 通过安静自己，专注呼吸，享受与上帝爱的同在</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1078">17:58</a> “Be Still and Know that I am God” 的字面意思与其背后深意&nbsp;</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1204">20:04</a> 萨提亚模式以及萨提亚冰山理论</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1493">24:53</a> 控制欲背后的不安全感来源：健康，婚姻，金钱</span></p><span></span><p><strong><span>本集提到的经文</span></strong></p><span></span><blockquote><strong><span>《箴言》 4章23节: </span></strong><em><span>“你要保守你心，胜过保守一切，因为生命的泉源（或：一生的果效）由心发出。”</span></em></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><strong><span>《以赛亚书》55章8-9节：</span></strong><span> </span><em><span>耶和华说：“我的意念并非你们的意念，我的道路并非你们的道路。正如天高过地，我的道路也高过你们的道路，我的意念也高过你们的意念。”</span></em></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><strong><span>《创世纪》2章7节：</span></strong><em><span>“耶和华神用地上的尘土造成人形，把生命之气吹进他的鼻孔里，那人就成了有生命的活人，</span></em><em><span>名叫亚当</span></em><em><span>。”</span></em></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><strong><span>《诗篇》46章10节：</span></strong><span> </span><em><span>祂说：“要安静（或：你们要休息），要知道我是上帝”</span></em></blockquote><span></span><p><strong><span>本集提到的希伯来文：</span></strong></p><span></span><blockquote><strong><span>Be Still: </span></strong><em><span>希伯来语是 </span></em><em><strong><span>Rapha</span></strong></em><em><span>，意思是“放松，沉下，放下，软弱”</span></em></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><strong><span>Know: </span></strong><em><span>希伯来语是 </span></em><em><strong><span>Yada</span></strong></em><em><span>, 意思是“有知识，有智慧，发现和分辨，透过体验来感知”</span></em></blockquote><span></span><p><strong><span>本集提到的学者/作者：</span></strong></p><span></span><blockquote><strong><span>Virginia Satir </span></strong><span>(维琴尼亚·萨提尔，1916-1988)，美国作家，知名的</span><strong><span>心理治疗师和家庭治疗师</span></strong><span>，也是美国家庭治疗(Family Therapy)发展史上最重要人物之一，她是第一代的家庭治疗师，从五十年代起已居于领导地位，向来被视为</span><strong><span>家庭治疗的先驱</span></strong><span>(Goldenberg, 1985)，甚至被誉为“家庭治疗的哥伦布”(McLendon, 1999)，意思是指家庭治疗是由她始创的。可见她在这方面的重大贡献，更因为她的建树良多，她的两所母校威斯康辛大学和芝加哥大学，曾分别颁授荣誉博士学位及“对人类杰出的贡献”金质奖章给她。</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span>萨提亚是最早提出在人际关系及治疗关系中，“人人平等，人皆有价值”的想法的人，她所建立的一套心理治疗方法，最大特点是着重提高个人的自尊、改善沟通及帮助人活得更</span><strong><span>“人性化”(Become more fully human)</span></strong><span>，而非只求消除“症状”(Symptoms)，治疗的最终目标是个人达致“身心整合，内外一致”(Congruece)。由于她的治疗法有很多地方与传统治疗方式回异，故被称为</span><strong><span>“萨提亚治疗模式”(The Satir Model, Banmen 1976, Satir 1991)。</span></strong></blockquote><span></span><figure><img src="https://image.xyzcdn.net/FmP84eK-_Wef2fLx81NrOm8HVcKr.png"></figure><span></span><blockquote><strong><span>萨提亚的冰山理论：</span></strong></blockquote><span></span><p><img src="https://bts-image.xyzcdn."></p>]]></description>
    <enclosure url="https://media.xyzcdn.net/lmtR1U-CSNxM2gOHOLxsZ6rZDgcj.m4a" length="62570479" type="audio/mp4"/>
    <itunes:duration>00:32:23</itunes:duration>
    <itunes:image href="https://image.xyzcdn.net/FkU6oMsXvSNGGNHU1SKX0VN4ods-.jpg"/>
    <itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>文明的暴力沟通，是如何毁掉亲密关系的？</title>
    <link>https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episode/663de35baf6f88d32f9759ba</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">663de35baf6f88d32f9759ba</guid>
    <pubDate>Fri, 10 May 2024 09:05:30 +0000</pubDate>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><span>好久不见，大家还好吗？这期播客，久别归来的猫三要跟大家分享“非暴力沟通”这个神奇又实用的人际关系大法。这里猫三结合了小说《那不勒斯四部曲》和HBO热剧《我的天才女友》的情节，给大家介绍非暴力沟通的基本概念和使用原则，让大家了解语言的使用是如何影响改变我们的人际关系，以及一生的命运的！</span></p><span></span><blockquote><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="316">05:16</a> 为什么“非暴力沟通”也叫爱的语言，生命的语言，和长颈鹿的语言？</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="405">06:45</a> 为什么非暴力沟通的本质是 Compassion Communication？ Compassion 这个词在古希伯来文，希腊语以及拉丁语里分别指什么？</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="782">13:02</a> 在《我的天才女友》里，语言是怎么影响两个出身相同的好朋友走向截然不同的人生的？</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1598">26:38</a> 为什么我们说出的话只是冰山的一角？冰山下面的90%又是什么？</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1698">28:18</a> 电影《The Break-Up》 两个片段分别是“暴力沟通”和“非暴力沟通”的经典案例</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2257">37:37</a> 非暴力沟通的三个原则：1）自我链接 2）真实表达 3）同理倾听</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2326">38:46</a> 诗歌《语言是窗户（否则，他们是墙）》</span></blockquote><span></span><blockquote><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2428">40:28</a> 我推荐的《非暴力沟通》书籍版本</span></blockquote><span></span><p><strong><span>本期提到经文古籍：</span></strong></p><span></span><ul><span>  </span><li><strong><span>"Compassion"第一次出现在《出埃及记》<a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2046">34:6</a> </span></strong><em><span>“耶和华在他面前宣告说：“耶和华，耶和华，是有怜悯有恩典的　神，不轻易发怒，并有丰盛的慈爱和诚实”</span></em></li><span>  </span><li><strong><span>所罗门王“智断亲子案”出自：《列王纪上》 <a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="196">3:16</a>-<a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="318">5:18</a></span></strong></li><span>  </span><li><strong><span>《以赛亚书》 <a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2955">49:15</a> </span></strong><em><strong><span>“</span></strong></em><em><span>妇人怎能忘记她吃奶的婴孩，不怜悯她亲生的儿子呢？即使她们可能忘记，我也不会忘记你。”</span></em></li><span>  </span><li><strong><span>《箴言》 <a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1047">17:27</a> </span></strong><em><span>“谨言慎行的有知识，温和冷静的有悟性”</span></em></li><span>  </span><li><strong><span>《箴言》 <a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1283">21:23</a></span></strong><span> </span><em><span>“管住口舌，免遭祸患”</span></em></li><span></span></ul><span></span><p><strong><span>本期提到的外语：</span></strong></p><span></span><ul><span>  </span><li><strong><span>RAKHUM（希伯来语）：</span></strong><span>怜悯</span></li><span>  </span><li><strong><span>RAKHAMIM（希伯来语）：</span></strong><span>有怜悯</span></li><span>  </span><li><strong><span>REKHEM（希伯来语）：</span></strong><span>母腹</span></li><span>  </span><li><strong><span>OIKTIRMOS （希腊语）：</span></strong><span>同情，悲悯，慈悲</span></li><span></span></ul><span></span><p><strong><span>本期提到的影视作品：</span></strong></p><span></span><ul><span>  </span><li><strong><span>The Passion of the Christ - 耶稣受难记</span></strong></li><span></span></ul><span></span><p><img src="https://image.xyzcdn.net/FuqUpG8mSpn3par4spshdOyeB72g.png"></p><span></span><ul><span>  </span><li><strong><span>The Break-up - 分手男女</span></strong></li><span></span></ul><span></span><figure><img src="https://image.xyzcdn.net/Fs5OERU-FJDbOqf-tSOmTg27B2Eu.jpg"></figure><span></span><ul><span>  </span><li><strong><span>My Brilliant Friend - 我的天才女友 （HBO剧）</span></strong></li><span></span></ul><span></span><figure><img src="https://image.xyzcdn.net/FhRbkW3WUV5nQ4O28CoZ0uFnW5VW.jpeg"></figure><span></span><p><strong><span>本期提到的书籍：</span></strong></p><span></span><ul><span>  </span><li><strong><span>《那不勒斯四部曲》- </span></strong><span>埃莱娜·费兰特</span></li><span></span></ul><span></span><figure><img src="https://image.xyzcdn.net/Fvh6cpDkqr6rsOf5PtCx_-A9YoBe.jpg"></figure><span></span><ul><span>  </span><li><strong><span>《生命不可承受之轻》 - </span></strong><span>米兰·昆德拉</span></li><span></span></ul><span></span><figure><img src="https://image.xyzcdn.net/FmnNBkTdw3iCQwxYgoskak1UeHDO.jpg"></figure><span></span><ul><span>  </span><li><strong><span>《非暴力沟通》- </span></strong><span>马歇尔.卢森堡</span></li><span></span></ul><span></span><figure><img src="https://image.xyzcdn.net/FnGLDPnnF0RFdKkxBffNS00iQVzT.jpg"></figure><span></span><p><strong><span>本期提到的音乐：</span></strong></p><span></span><ul><span>  </span><li><strong><span>"Words are windows, or they are walls" - </span></strong><span>Ruth Adeline Bebermeyer</span></li><span></span></ul><span></span><p><strong><span>本期提到的诗歌：</span></strong></p><span></span><ul><span>  </span><li><strong><span>"Words are windows, or they are walls" </span></strong><span>- Ruth Adeline Bebermeyer</span></li><span></span></ul><span></span><p><em><span>I felt so sentenced by your words,</span><br><span>I felt so judged and sent away,</span><br><span>Before I go I’ve got to know</span><br><span>Was that what you mean to say?</span></em></p><span></span><p><em><span>Before I rise to my defense,</span><br><span>Before I speak in hurt or fear,</span><br><span>Before I build that wall of words,</span><br><span>Tell me, did I really hear?</span></em></p><span></span><p><em><span>Words are windows, or they’re walls.</span><br><span>They sentence us, or set us free.</span><br><span>When I speak and when I hear,</span><br><span>Let the love light shine through me.</span></em></p><span></span><p><em><span>There are things I needed to say,</span><br><span>Things that meant so much to me,</span><br><span>If my words don’t made me clear,</span><br><span>Would you have help me to be free?</span></em></p><span></span><p><em><span>If I seemed to put you down,</span><br><span>If you felt I didn’t care,</span><br><span>Try to listen through my words</span><br><span>To the feelings that we shared.</span></em></p>]]></description>
